# Narset's Reversal: "You may choose new targets for the copy." Bot1's Lightning Bolt is aimed at Bot2; the copy is
# given a new target, Bot1 itself (CR 707.10c): Bot1 takes 3 and Bot2 none. The original returns to Bot1's hand and
# was never cast again, so it deals nothing. The other answer (keeping Bot2) is
# narsets-reversal-copies-your-bolt-keeps-its-target-and-returns-the-original.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Narset's Reversal
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Hand.Narset's Reversal.Cast(Stack.Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

